    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43486" root="&#xA;                        متع&#xA;                    " body-key="m1">
                        
                            1
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَتَعَ النَّهَارُ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>The day became advanced, the
sun being high,</i> (S, K,) <i>before the declining of the
sun from the meridian.</i> (K.)
. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَتَّعَهُ</span>
                        <i>He</i> (God) <i>made him to live.</i> (Bd in
xi. 3.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلّا</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَتَّعَهَا</span>
                        <i>He gave her a gift
after divorce.</i> (K.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَتَّهَا بِكَذَا</span>
                        <i>He gave
her</i> (a divorced wife) <i>such a thing.</i> (Msb.)

